# Migration baseline
#
# Migrations are append-only: rewriting one that a database already ran leaves
# that database unmigratable. scripts/ci/migration-history-check.sh enforces
# that and permits an exception only when this file changes in the same diff,
# which is how a pack that has never been applied anywhere gets consolidated
# before its first publication. Updating this file asserts, with the evidence
# below, that nothing could have applied the migrations being rewritten.
#
# This is not a routine step. Once a migration has shipped in a runtime image or
# reached any database, it is immutable and stays immutable; cd.yml enforces
# that separately against the published image and has no escape.

generation: 2

## generation 2 - 2026-08-03

Consolidated the PostgreSQL outbox pack from 000001..000004 into a single
000001_postgres_outbox.sql holding the final schema. The three follow-ups were
corrections to a pack introduced in the same week: materializing ordering_ready,
adding the append notification and pending index, and applying the measured
storage parameters and index consolidation.

Evidence that nothing had applied them:

- the ghcr package carried no `migration-history` tag, so no runtime image had
  ever published a migration corpus, and CD's publish jobs were skipping;
- the only published image predated the outbox pack entirely;
- `migrations/` is not in `template-owned.paths`, so it is copied into a service
  once at `template-init` and never synced afterwards, leaving derived checkouts
  with their own frozen copies that this change cannot reach;
- every file in the pack was authored within the same week and no release had
  been cut from it.

